{
  "name": "two-cabs",
  "title": "Two cabs in parallel",
  "description": "Two cabinets. Rounds run in simultaneous pairs (1+2, 3+4, ... 9+10) whose tappers are disjoint, so every player taps exactly once per time slot. Each round's drafters and gamblers are the other round's tappers, drafting and predicting in parallel at the start of the slot. The event takes half as long.",
  "critique": "No waiting at all and perfectly even late-round value, by construction. Mixing is coarser: every slot splits the room into two fixed halves, which raises the co-occurrence floor to 1250 (met exactly). By pigeonhole some pairs must be extreme, and the minimum is reached: 5 pairs never tap together; every other pair taps together 1-4 times. Gambling is also less even, since you only ever gamble on the other half of the room.",
